{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "comment": "X-02 §6.3: the host's op journal compares a request with the stored op by fingerprint (SHA-256 of method || 0x00 || the params without session and operation_id) and by account. Same operation_id, fingerprint and account: replay. Same operation_id with another fingerprint or account: operation_reused. fingerprint_input is the exact bytes hashed, as UTF-8. A secret (account.create's password) is never part of the fingerprint. account.create's row also keeps a create-time verifier of its password (a copy of the Argon2id PHC string the create produced, same salt and parameters, no separate key; the host stores it and verifies a replay through its Argon2 pool in move 2b), never the account's current hash; 'password_verifier' says whether the retry's password matches it, and a mismatch is operation_reused even when the fingerprint and account match. 'bootstrap': bootstrap's fingerprint is its method, login and hq_operation_id, never the password, the TLS pair or operation_id. Each retry of the stored bootstrap says whether its fingerprint is the same and what the replay gets, checked in this order: the login and password as a sign-in (not_authorized), then the fingerprint (operation_reused), then the pair (tls_mismatch); otherwise it replays. Logins (account.create's and bootstrap's) are fingerprinted normalized (§6.2: NFC, case-folded): every login in these vectors is already in that form, and the fingerprint functions use the login as given, so callers pass it normalized; the host normalizes before fingerprinting in move 2b.",
