  "tls_set": {
    "comment": "X-02 §6.2, §6.3: tls.set's fingerprint fields are exactly {\"cert_der_sha256\", \"key_der_sha256\"}, the SHA-256 as lowercase hex of the DER in cert's first CERTIFICATE block and in key's first PRIVATE KEY, RSA PRIVATE KEY or EC PRIVATE KEY block, never the pair itself; session and operation_id are excluded as for every op. The certificate and keys are synthetic, made with openssl for these vectors (P-256 and a 512-bit RSA key, CN=mac.local and CN=ca.local); the expected hashes were computed with openssl (x509, pkey, ec and rsa -outform DER | sha256sum), not by this crate. A body is strict standard base64 (spaces, tabs, CR and LF aside); a pair with no such block, or a body that doesn't decode, has no fingerprint: the host refuses it as tls_invalid, unstored, before it would fingerprint it, and fingerprint_fields() fails on it.",
